    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Linear Pottery culture spread about 1,500 km along the rivers in 360 years, about 4 km a year, and represents a major event in the spread of agriculture in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</li><li>Its longhouses, 5.5 to 7.0 m wide and sometimes 45 m long, were the largest free-standing buildings in the world at the time.</li><li>Mass graves such as the Talheim Death Pit and Herxheim overturned an earlier view of the culture as peaceful and unfortified.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>A 2022 study of residues from over 4,300 vessels at 70 LBK sites found traces of milk at about 65% of them, some dating as early as 7,400 years ago.</p></aside>
    </section>

